      {
        "body": "{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","max_tokens":1024,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive"},"output_config":{"effort":"medium","format":{"type":"json_schema","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string","enum":["connect_club","go_live","approve_club","reject_club","stop_messages","stop_ratings","resume_messages","resume_ratings","recruit_blast","partner_ask","rating_progress","intro_messages","question","other"]},"intro":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer"}},"club_ref":{"type":"string"},"confidence":{"type":"number"},"reasoning":{"type":"string"}},"required":["intent","intro","club_ref","confidence","reasoning"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"system":[{"type":"text","text":"Someone sent MatchTime, their football club's WhatsApp bot, the private message under \\"THE DM\\". Above it you get who they are (their clubs, whether they organise each one, and whether it is live or still setting up), the partner clubs of the clubs they organise when there are any, the time now, and what MatchTime said to them: the message they swipe-replied to, or else MatchTime's recent messages to them, each with when it was sent and what it was about.\\n\\nSay what the message asks MatchTime to do. You never do it and never answer it, and you never decide who may ask: MatchTime checks who the sender is before it acts. Pick one:\\n\\nSetting a club up:\\n- \\"connect_club\\": they send MatchTime the message from the sign-up page that connects their club to MatchTime, with the code it gave them (\\"Connect Riverside FC, code 7KQ2\\"), however they word it.\\n- \\"go_live\\": an organiser tells MatchTime to start their club now, as MatchTime's setup message asks (\\"reply GO\\").\\n- \\"approve_club\\": they tell MatchTime to approve a club that asked to join. \\"club_ref\\" is the club's ref exactly as they wrote it (a short code of letters and digits such as 7KQ2), or \\"\\" when they wrote none.\\n- \\"reject_club\\": they tell MatchTime to reject a club that asked to join, with \\"club_ref\\" as for \\"approve_club\\".\\n\\nTheir own messages from MatchTime:\\n- \\"stop_messages\\": stop messaging them, about everything or about everything but payments.\\n- \\"stop_ratings\\": stop only the rating and Man of the Match messages.\\n- \\"resume_messages\\": message them again about everything.\\n- \\"resume_ratings\\": send them the rating and Man of the Match messages again.\\n- \\"intro_messages\\": send THEM MatchTime's ready-made introduction messages, the ones they paste into other WhatsApp groups. There are three: 1 for football groups that do not know MatchTime, 2 for groups that are not about football (inviting people to the player pool), 3 for clubs already using MatchTime (its new features). \\"intro\\" lists the ones they picked, by number or by description; when they want all of them, or pick none, it is [].\\n\\nAn organiser's instruction:\\n- \\"recruit_blast\\": CONTACT the club's own players who are not signed up for the next match and invite them.\\n- \\"partner_ask\\": ask ANOTHER club, a partner club or the other groups whether anyone can play, whether a club is named or not.\\n- \\"rating_progress\\": say HOW MANY have sent their ratings or Man of the Match votes for the match just played, or WHO has not.\\n\\nEverything else:\\n- \\"question\\": they ask MatchTime something, with or without a question mark: the next match (when, where, who is in), their own stats, ratings or payments, results, how to rate, sign up or drop out, or anything else. Asking about a message MatchTime sent them (\\"what time?\\" to an invite) is a question too.\\n- \\"other\\": saying they can or cannot play, answering something MatchTime asked them (a yes, a no, a number, a name, \\"paid\\"), thanks, news, chat or a complaint.\\n\\nWho is told to do the work decides it. Telling the PLAYERS to do something, describing what players said or did, reporting a fact (a drop-out, a shortage), talking about another club, thanking, complaining or chatting is \\"other\\", however often the message says players, ratings, DM, message, stop, everyone, squad, intro, code, approve or a club's name. Asking MatchTime to REMIND players is not asking for the rating tally, asking it to post or say something to the group is not asking for the intro messages, and asking what a code is or where to find one is a \\"question\\", not \\"connect_club\\".\\n\\nRead the message against what MatchTime said to them: the message they swipe-replied to, or else the newest recent one. A short follow-up such as \\"who's left?\\" or \\"and the MoM?\\" answering MatchTime's rating update is \\"rating_progress\\". \\"Yes, approve it\\" or \\"reject that one\\" answering MatchTime's message about a club waiting to join is \\"approve_club\\" or \\"reject_club\\", with \\"club_ref\\" \\"\\" unless they wrote the ref. A bare answer (\\"yes\\", \\"no\\", \\"done\\", \\"ok\\", \\"👍\\", \\"stop\\", \\"wait\\") to anything else MatchTime asked them (an invite, a bench place, a fee to confirm, a request to rate teammates) is \\"other\\". A message that is itself one of the instructions stays one, whatever it replies to.\\n\\nExamples (English | Turkish):\\nconnect_club: \\"Connect Riverside FC, code 7KQ2\\" | \\"Riverside FC kulübünü bağla, kod 7KQ2\\"; \\"here's my code 7KQ3, please link our group\\" | \\"kodum 7KQ3, grubumuzu bağlar mısın\\"\\ngo_live: \\"GO\\" | \\"BAŞLA\\"; \\"go live\\" | \\"başla\\"\\napprove_club: \\"APPROVE 7KQ2\\" | \\"ONAYLA 7KQ2\\" (club_ref \\"7KQ2\\"); \\"yes approve 9XT4\\" | \\"9XT4 onaylandı\\" (club_ref \\"9XT4\\"); \\"approve it\\" | \\"onayla\\" (club_ref \\"\\")\\nreject_club: \\"REJECT 7KQ2\\" | \\"REDDET 7KQ2\\" (club_ref \\"7KQ2\\"); \\"reject that one\\" | \\"bunu reddet\\" (club_ref \\"\\")\\nstop_messages: \\"do not message me on any topic but payment\\" | \\"ödeme dışında bana mesaj atma\\"; \\"stop messaging me\\" | \\"bana mesaj atmayın\\"; \\"only payment messages please\\" | \\"sadece ödeme mesajları gelsin\\"; \\"STOP\\" | \\"bildirimleri kapat\\"\\nstop_ratings: \\"no more rating messages please\\" | \\"puanlama mesajı göndermeyin\\"; \\"stop sending me the MoM vote\\" | \\"maçın adamı oylamasını atma\\"\\nresume_messages: \\"start messages\\" | \\"mesajları aç\\"; \\"you can message me again\\" | \\"tekrar mesaj atabilirsin\\"\\nresume_ratings: \\"start ratings\\" | \\"puanlamayı aç\\"; \\"send me the rating links again\\" | \\"puanlama linklerini yine gönder\\"\\nintro_messages: \\"send me the category 1 intro message\\" | \\"kategori 1 tanıtım mesajını gönder\\" (intro [1]); \\"the player pool invite for my running group\\" | \\"koşu grubum için oyuncu havuzu daveti\\" (intro [2]); \\"the new features message for clubs on MatchTime\\" | \\"kategori 3 tanıtım mesajını gönder\\" (intro [3]); \\"send me all the intro messages\\" | \\"tüm tanıtım mesajlarını gönder\\" (intro [])\\nrecruit_blast: \\"DM everyone who played in the last 5 matches and invite them\\" | \\"son 5 maçta oynayan herkese yaz, davet et\\"; \\"we need a couple more for tuesday, can you message the recent lads\\" | \\"salıya iki kişi eksik, son gelenlere mesaj atar mısın\\"; \\"we're short, round some players up\\" | \\"eksiğimiz var, birkaç oyuncu topla\\"\\npartner_ask: \\"ask Sutton if anyone can play tonight\\" | \\"Sutton'a sor bakalım oynayan var mı\\"; \\"can you ask the partner clubs for a player\\" | \\"partner kulüplere sorar mısın, bir oyuncu lazım\\"; \\"try the other groups for one more\\" | \\"diğer gruplara sor, oynayacak biri var mı\\"\\nrating_progress: \\"who hasn't rated yet?\\" | \\"kim daha puan vermedi?\\"; \\"how many have picked a MoM so far\\" | \\"kaç kişi maçın adamını seçti\\"; \\"is everyone done rating\\" | \\"herkes puanladı mı\\"\\nquestion: \\"who's playing tuesday?\\" | \\"salı kimler var\\"; \\"what time is kick off\\" | \\"maç saat kaçta\\"; \\"what time?\\" | \\"saat kaçta?\\" answering an invite; \\"how much do I owe\\" | \\"ne kadar borcum var\\"; \\"what's my rating\\" | \\"puanım kaç\\"; \\"where do I find the code?\\" | \\"kodu nerede bulurum?\\"\\nother: \\"please do not forget to rate the players via the link from Matchtime DM'ed to you\\" (it tells the players); \\"Najib is out. We need one more player.\\" | \\"Ahmet yok. Bir kişi lazım.\\" (it reports a drop); \\"the lads keep asking me to DM them the ratings link\\" (it describes a situation); \\"Sutton were great last week\\" | \\"Sutton geçen hafta çok iyi oynadı\\"; \\"can you remind everyone to rate the players\\" | \\"herkese puan vermeyi hatırlat\\" (a reminder); \\"introduce yourself to the group\\" | \\"gruba kendini tanıt\\" (a post to the group); \\"the gate code is 4829\\" | \\"kapı kodu 4829\\"; \\"IN\\" | \\"varım\\"; \\"sorry can't make tuesday\\" | \\"salı gelemiyorum\\"; \\"go on then\\" | \\"olur, gelirim\\"; \\"thanks\\" | \\"sağ ol\\"; \\"dur\\" answering a fee to confirm; \\"done 👍\\" answering a request to rate teammates\\n\\nIf you are not at least 80% sure, choose \\"other\\". A wrong \\"go_live\\" starts a club before its organiser is ready; a wrong \\"approve_club\\" or \\"reject_club\\" decides a club's request the owner did not decide; a wrong stop silences someone who wanted the messages; a wrong \\"recruit_blast\\" sends an unwanted private message to up to 27 real people; a wrong \\"partner_ask\\" troubles another club's organisers; a wrong \\"other\\" costs one re-typed message.\\n\\nOutput STRICT JSON only, no markdown, no fences:\\n{\\"intent\\": \\"connect_club\\" | \\"go_live\\" | \\"approve_club\\" | \\"reject_club\\" | \\"stop_messages\\" | \\"stop_ratings\\" | \\"resume_messages\\" | \\"resume_ratings\\" | \\"intro_messages\\" | \\"recruit_blast\\" | \\"partner_ask\\" | \\"rating_progress\\" | \\"question\\" | \\"other\\", \\"intro\\": [<the category numbers, each 1, 2 or 3>], \\"club_ref\\": \\"<the ref as written, or empty>\\", \\"confidence\\": <number 0..1>, \\"reasoning\\": \\"<max 100 chars>\\"}\\nExactly these five keys, one object, nothing after it. \\"intro\\" is [] for every intent but \\"intro_messages\\", and \\"club_ref\\" is \\"\\" for every intent but \\"approve_club\\" and \\"reject_club\\".","cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Their clubs: FNF (player, live)\\nSender: Someone\\nNOW: Saturday 7 November 2026, 10:00 (club time, London)\\nMATCHTIME'S RECENT MESSAGES TO THEM: none in the last 14 days.\\nTHE DM:\\nwhat time is kick off?"}]}",
        "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
        "raw": true,
      },
      {
        "label": "extractor:question",
        "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
        "schema": "3326dfac6034fccd",
        "system": "332f6f65c72ee273",
        "user": "NOW: Saturday 7 November 2026, 10:00 (club time, London)

THE MESSAGE (from (unknown), who tagged the bot):
what time is kick off?",
      },
      {
        "label": "dm-qa",
        "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
        "schema": "74234e98afe7498f",
        "system": "3f26110c7b9072f1",
        "user": "CONTEXT (everything you may use; nothing else exists for you):
GROUP: FNF

UPCOMING MATCH: none scheduled right now.

YOUR STATS:
- Games played: 0/0 (0% attendance)
- Average rating: — (squad avg —)
- Man of the Match: 0
- Record: 0W 0D 0L
- Form (last 5): — (steady)

YOUR PAYMENTS (this player's own; you know nothing about anyone else's payments):
- This club does not run payments through MatchTime. For money questions, ask the organiser.

WHAT MATCHTIME SAID TO THEM:
NOW: Saturday 7 November 2026, 10:00 (club time, London)
MATCHTIME'S RECENT MESSAGES TO THEM: none in the last 14 days.

The player asks:
what time is kick off?

Answer per your rules.",
      },
    ],
    "response": {
      "handled": "dm-qa",
      "ok": true,
    },
    "status": 200,
    "writes": [
      {
        "args": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "dm",
            "orgId": "org-fnf",
            "phone": "447700900311",
            "priority": 1,
            "text": "{}",
          },
        },
        "call": "botJob.create",
      },
    ],
  },
}
`;

