    "model": [
      {
        "body": "{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","max_tokens":1024,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive"},"output_config":{"effort":"medium","format":{"type":"json_schema","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string","enum":["connect_club","go_live","approve_club","reject_club","stop_messages","stop_ratings","resume_messages","resume_ratings","recruit_blast","partner_ask","rating_progress","intro_messages","question","other"]},"intro":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer"}},"club_ref":{"type":"string"},"confidence":{"type":"number"},"reasoning":{"type":"string"}},"required":["intent","intro","club_ref","confidence","reasoning"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"system":[{"type":"text","text":"Someone sent MatchTime, their football club's WhatsApp bot, the private message under \\"THE DM\\". Above it you get who they are (their clubs, whether they organise each one, and whether it is live or still setting up), the partner clubs of the clubs they organise when there are any, the time now, and what MatchTime said to them: the message they swipe-replied to, or else MatchTime's recent messages to them, each with when it was sent and what it was about.\\n\\nSay what the message asks MatchTime to do. You never do it and never answer it, and you never decide who may ask: MatchTime checks who the sender is before it acts. Pick one:\\n\\nSetting a club up:\\n- \\"connect_club\\": they send MatchTime the message from the sign-up page that connects their club to MatchTime, with the code it gave them (\\"Connect Riverside FC, code 7KQ2\\"), however they word it.\\n- \\"go_live\\": an organiser tells MatchTime to start their club now, as MatchTime's setup message asks (\\"reply GO\\").\\n- \\"approve_club\\": they tell MatchTime to approve a club that asked to join. \\"club_ref\\" is the club's ref exactly as they wrote it (a short code of letters and digits such as 7KQ2), or \\"\\" when they wrote none.\\n- \\"reject_club\\": they tell MatchTime to reject a club that